WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome back
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.133
Bridget Everett, music from

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.634
Red Hot Chili Peppers
is on the way,

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:07.167
but first, it's time
to play "Box of Lies."

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:09.267
[ Cheering and applause ]
The game,

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:10.601
if you don't know,
works like this.

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:13.834
We have nine mystery boxes
containing who knows what.

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:17.000
These are mystery items
in the mystery boxes.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.400
Hugh will pick a box.
He will remove the object

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.267
and describe it to his opponent,
which is me,

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.234
and then I have to guess
if he was lying

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:26.133
or telling the truth
about what's in the box.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.100
And, based
on your customs story,

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.200
it seems like I should win
this pretty easily.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.734
[ Laughter ]
-Just take it now.

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:33.767
-And we'll play two rounds.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.501
Loser has to eat a rat, okay?

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.234
[ Laughter ]
-Yay! Awesome.
-Alright, here we go.

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:38.634
You pick first.
You're the guest.

00:00:38.634 --> 00:00:40.467
Go crazy.
-Alright, let's go for it.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:41.667
1, 2, or 3?
-3!

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:44.767
3? 3 it is. I heard 3.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:47.667
People really have a strong
opinion on a number.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:50.367
[ Laughter ]
-And, while I'm pulling
this out,

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:52.534
I know we're playing a game,
but Ahmir, Questlove,

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:54.400
that movie "Summer of Soul"?
You have to see it.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.901
Won the Oscar
for Best Documentary.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:59.000
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.767
-Ooh!
[ Laughing ]

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:06.701
Oh, hoh, ooh, yes.

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:09.901
[ Laughter ]
I like it.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.267
Oh, I really like it.

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:12.234
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:13.701
-You can keep it, probably.

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:15.667
[ Laughter ]
-Uh, you know what?

00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:16.801
I'm not going to keep this one.

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:18.167
-Oh.
-This kind of -- Yeah.

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:20.067
-Okay.
-Scare small children.

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:22.200
[ Laughter ]
Alright, so, wow.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.334
So it's jelly,
like a jelly mold,

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.100
circular jelly,
and, inside it...

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.234
♪♪

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:31.801
...I'm presuming,

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:33.434
is fake poo.

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:35.968
[ Laughter ]
-Ooh, interesting.

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:39.501
-Mm.
-Now, I'm going to say,

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:41.501
not necessarily based
on your delivery,

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.367
but, based on the fact that
that would be

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:47.367
an exceptionally disgusting
thing to put in a box...

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:48.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:51.234
...that you, Hugh Jackman,

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:53.300
are lying.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.934
-You're accusing me of lying?

00:01:54.934 --> 00:01:55.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:58.234
Damn it!
I'm really bad at lying!

00:01:58.234 --> 00:02:00.334
[ Laughter ]
[ Rimshot ]
Damn it!

00:02:00.334 --> 00:02:03.234
-What do we have here?

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:04.701
Ooh, a little diorama.

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:06.100
-By the way, I am keeping that.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.734
It's so good.
-Oh, look at that, yeah.

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:09.567
Wow! look at that.
-That is so good.

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:11.000
-You're about to kill
Professor X.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.601
[ Laughter ]
That doesn't seem in keeping

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:15.133
with the canon of the --
-Giving him a nice close shave.

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:16.501
-I don't know what we do
with these now.

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:17.901
-I don't know what we do,
either.

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.467
-Alright, now,
it's time for me to pick a box.

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:20.968
-Can I keep this, by the way?
-I am going to take

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:23.167
number...
-5!

00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:25.100
-Your opinions are not welcome.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:27.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:28.000
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.501
I'm going with number 6

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:31.601
because it's the closest one.
Alright?

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:32.801
-Alright.
-Alright.

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:34.701
♪♪

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:36.501
Alright. Okay.

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:38.968
♪♪

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:40.868
Alright.

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:43.133
This is --

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:44.868
Show it to the audience.

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:47.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:51.801
This is a cake

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:56.367
with shrimp cocktail
on top of it

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:58.267
and it says...

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.901
[ Laughter ]
...on it.

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:05.501
-[ Laughing ] It's just --

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:08.501
just way too good to be true.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.067
That's way too good to be true

00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:13.000
and I have a funny feeling,
Jimmy,

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.200
that you may want to show that
you're a better liar than me.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.634
That's just my gut.

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:19.067
I'm sensing a little --
-Why would anyone want

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:21.033
to show that?
In fact...

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.634
-Everybody is.
-...something I'd keep
quiet, probably.

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:25.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:27.267
♪♪

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:28.901
-Jimmy, you're lying.

00:03:28.901 --> 00:03:30.033
I know you're lying.

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:32.868
-I would never lie to you,
Hugh Jackman.

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:34.434
[ Sad trombone, rimshot ]

00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:35.701
In fact, it's this.

00:03:35.701 --> 00:03:37.501
[ Applause ]
-Wow!

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:39.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:40.367
-I know.
It's weird, right?

00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:42.801
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:44.133
-Is that game over?

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:45.968
-I think the game's over.
-Is that game over?

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:48.067
-I think I won.
-I told you.

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:49.167
I'm the worst liar.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:50.901
[ Rimshot ]
I can't even spot a lie.

00:03:50.901 --> 00:03:52.534
-You got a show to go to.

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:54.701
Hugh Jackman is
in "The Music Man."

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:57.300
You will never get tickets
to this, so forget about it,

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.167
[ Laughter ]
but, on the off chance you do,

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:00.834
it's at the
Winter Garden Theatre.

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:02.734
-And, if you come,
I want you to know,

00:04:02.734 --> 00:04:04.567
somewhere on the stage,
this will be there,

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:06.334
and I'm not lying. Somewhere.
-Oh. that's wonderful.

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.667
[ Cheering and applause ]
And, Hugh,

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:10.968
I'm going to tell you that

00:04:10.968 --> 00:04:12.501
we're going to send this
to Ryan Reynolds,

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:13.901
for his house.
-Thank you so much.

00:04:13.901 --> 00:04:14.968
[ Applause ]
-Hugh Jackman, everybody.

